@startuml
title Student Feature — Component Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor Student
actor Teacher

component "Single React/Vite App\nStudent pages and forms" as Web
component "Student Web Adapters\nHTTP / draft Socket client" as StudentClient
component "Shared Foundation Web\nRouter / Layout / SessionStateClient" as FoundationWeb

component "Express API Router" as Api
component "Student Feature Module" as StudentModule {
  component "Student HTTP API" as StudentApi
  component "Cookie Identity Resolver\nActorContext adapter" as Identity
  component "Enrollment / Team Service" as TeamService
  component "Draft Service" as DraftService
  component "Submission Service" as SubmissionService
  component "Student Winner Resolver" as WinnerService
  component "Student Result Projection" as ResultProjection
  component "Teacher Leader Transfer\nT004 integration proposal" as LeaderTransfer
  component "StudentTrustedEndCoordinator\nT004 integration proposal" as EndCoordinator
  component "Student Draft Socket Events" as DraftSocket
  component "Student Presence and Failover" as Presence
}
component "Foundation Module" as Foundation {
  component "Session Query / Current Target" as ReadService
  component "Lifecycle Transaction Service\nexisting End with supplied Result" as Lifecycle
  component "Foundation session-state events" as StateEvents
}
component "Teacher Feature Backend" as TeacherModule
component "Server Composition Root" as Composition
interface "Proposed internal callback port\n(roundId) => Result | null" as WinnerPort
database "Shared SQLite\nFoundation entities + Student tables" as DB

Student --> Web
Teacher --> TeacherModule
Web --> FoundationWeb
Web --> StudentClient
StudentClient --> Api : same-origin HTTP
StudentClient --> DraftSocket : student:draft:* via WebSocket
FoundationWeb --> StateEvents : session:watch / state snapshots\nvia Student-authenticated WebSocket
Api --> StudentApi
StudentApi --> Identity : resolve verified cookie actor
StudentApi --> TeamService
StudentApi --> DraftService
StudentApi --> SubmissionService
StudentApi --> ResultProjection
StudentApi --> ReadService : reuse Activity Code / current-target reads
DraftSocket --> Identity
DraftSocket --> DraftService : authorized watch/edit
DraftSocket --> Presence : authenticated socket lifecycle\nand authorized re-subscription
Presence --> DB : read join order / atomically update leader
Presence --> StudentClient : committed membership invalidation\nverified Team sockets in any phase
LeaderTransfer ..> Presence : reuse membership publication after commit
TeamService --> DB : Participant / TeamLeader / credential mapping
DraftService --> DB : Team × Round draft / answers
SubmissionService --> DB : canonical Submission / answers + draft lock
WinnerService --> DB : accepted order in caller transaction
ResultProjection --> DB : persisted Result / winning answers
ReadService --> DB
Lifecycle --> DB
TeacherModule ..> LeaderTransfer : proposed transferLeaderByTeacher call
LeaderTransfer ..> DB : proposed atomic leader reassignment
TeacherModule ..> EndCoordinator : proposed single endRound call
EndCoordinator ..> Lifecycle : proposed Foundation internal port
Lifecycle ..> WinnerPort : proposed callback inside write transaction
WinnerService ..|> WinnerPort : implemented resolver, wiring pending
Lifecycle --> StateEvents : publish only after commit
StateEvents --> Web : existing Foundation state contract
Composition ..> EndCoordinator : proposed injection
Composition ..> Lifecycle
Composition ..> WinnerService : proposed End wiring

note bottom of StudentModule
First-time join after first Active is allowed only into an existing Team.
Student never creates Teams; existing members cannot transfer after first Active.
Student owns enrollment, opaque identity mapping, leader state, drafts,
acceptedOrder creation and Student-only result projection.
The `student_session` HttpOnly cookie uses Path=/ for Student HTTP and /socket.io;
the server validates handshake Origin and derives identity from the cookie mapping.
end note

note bottom of StudentClient
Student UI uses acknowledged HTTP edits per Blank;
DraftClient reconciles HTTP results and versioned Socket notifications.
Focused and failed local input is preserved until saved/confirmed.
Identity is restored through the opaque Cookie; no browser token storage.
end note

note bottom of Foundation
Existing public HTTP/DTO/Socket.IO contracts remain unchanged.
Foundation and Student share one SQLite connection.
The planned internal End callback is gated by T004; Foundation will not import Student.
State publication is dispatched after commit.
end note

note right of TeacherModule
Foundation currently grants only read/watch capabilities.
team:leader:transfer and round:end are new proposed ActorContext strings,
not existing Foundation permissions; Teacher middleware must issue them after auth.
The proposed Teacher integration calls one Student End coordinator.
Teacher owns login/UI; Student selects the winner.
end note
@enduml
